  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-OiC Coordination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam in Cambodia plays very important role in coordination with relevant stakeholders. Oxfam manages grants and maintains partnership with 6 partners including FACT, MVI, NRD, 3SPN, Royal University of Agriculture, and National Committee for Disaster Management.Oxfam will provide capacity building to partners by building partner&apos;s understanding on the project overview, principles and compliances. Oxfam will monitor the project progresses against the planned activities ensuring quality deliverables and financial accountability.

At the beginning Oxfam in Cambodia organized consultation meeting with stakeholders ranging from communities, sub-national administrations and NGO partners to define issues and needs and project interventions as well as defining role and responsibilities of project stakeholders.

OiC will conduct partner&apos;s assessment (PRISMA) and adminster grant to partners according to Oxfam&apos;s granting systems and procedures.

Oxfam in Cambodia will also coordinate with other countries shared border with Cambodia to improve coordination and information sharing of climate hazards and hydrological date sharing between the neighboring countries.

Oxfam in Cambodia ensures safeguarding and project financial and narratives submitted to PMU on time.</narrative>
  </description>
